      ":question/difficulty": ":question.difficulty/hard",
      ":question/worked-solution": "First, notice that both $3a$ and $-a$ must be parallel to $a$.\n\nNow, for the vector $3a$ we have the following:\n\n- The magnitude of $3a$ is $3$ times the magnitude of $a$.\n- Vectors $a$ and $3a$ have the same direction since the factor $3$ is positive.\n\nNext, for the vector $-a$ we have the following:\n\n- The magnitude of $-a$ is $1$ times the magnitude of $a$.\n- Vectors $a$ and $-a$ have opposite directions since the factor $-1$ is negative.\n\nThe required vectors are shown below.\n\n![](images/d6/d6c501b98e6eb5b998b6ebf822ec33e23dc1e67c01e3424e571ac19ded016a9a.png)"
